  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader who lowers Réglages › Taille du texte, I want the message text to stay at or above 11 pt, so that the reading screen stays legible, as the lists do since #1157 (PR #1236).\n\n### Observed (code reading, PR #1236 review)\n\nThe reader scales through `factor` in a script (`ReaderWebController+Scripts.swift:88`) and `reader.css` (`:31, 100, 130, 205`) has no floor. At 70 % and the default Dynamic Type size: message body 0.7 × 15 = 10.5 px, dates 10.1, quote headers 8.9, badges 8.3.\n\n### Scope\n\n- A floor on the em base or per element (`max(11px, …)`), same rule as `TextScale.pointSize` after #1236: sizes at 100 % and above unchanged.\n- Legacy never goes below 100 % (`Common.swift:314-322` @ `87fe0d1c`): the 70–130 % range is SwiftHFR's, no ledger entry.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] At 70 %, every reader text (body, dates, quote headers, badges) computes to ≥ 11 px, shown by an app-hosted WebKit test that fails first.\n- [ ] 100 % and above unchanged.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
